  "title": "Cnemaspis boulengerii",
  "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cnemaspis_boulengerii",
  "revision": 1376672770,
  "sections": [
   {
    "h": null,
    "level": 1,
    "paras": [
     "Cnemaspis boulengerii, also known commonly as Boulenger's rock gecko or the Con Dao round eyed gecko, is a species of lizard in the family Gekkonidae. The species is endemic to Côn Sơn Island (also called Pulo Condore) in southern Vietnam."
    ]
   },
   {
    "h": "Etymology",
    "level": 2,
    "paras": [
     "The specific name, boulengerii, is in honor of Belgian-born British herpetologist George Albert Boulenger."
    ]
   },
   {
    "h": "Habitat",
    "level": 2,
    "paras": [
     "The preferred natural habitats of C. boulengerii are forest, rocky areas, and caves."
    ]
   },
   {
    "h": "Description",
    "level": 2,
    "paras": [
     "Dorsally, C. boulengerii is tan, with a few large roundish black spots on the shoulders and nape. Ventrally it is grayish white. The maximum recorded snout-to-vent length (SVL) is 6.9 cm (2.7 in). The tail is about 10% longer than SVL."
    ]
   },
   {
    "h": "Reproduction",
    "level": 2,
    "paras": [
     "C. boulengerii is oviparous."
    ]
   }
  ]
 }
